      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Traffic Counter\n\nA retro pixel-styled offline browser application for tracking vehicular traffic (Car, Bus, and Bike).\n\n## Features\n\n- **Category Buttons**: Clickable and keyboard-accessible buttons for Car, Bus, and Bike.\n- **Real-time Statistics**: Shows total volume alongside individual category counts and exact percentages.\n- **Progress Indicators**: Pixelated color-coded bars corresponding to each vehicle's share of total traffic.\n- **Sequential Undo**: An Undo button that removes the most recently added vehicle, updating counts and percentages instantly.\n- **Pixel Art Visuals**: Pixel-art vehicle icons drawn procedurally using the HTML5 `<canvas>` API with no external image files or web fonts.\n- **Accessibility**: Semantic HTML layout, ARIA labels, live feedback updates, and high-contrast visible focus rings.\n- **Responsive Design**: Adapts cleanly to mobile viewports down to 360px.\n\n## Running the Project\n\n1. Open `index.html` directly in any modern web browser.\n2. No build steps, web servers, external dependencies, or network connections are required.\n",
